[2026-03-14T22:08:58.615Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvHEjsJRRznDrDPZGs2XPw","type":"tool_result","content":"  2300→#### Test: Create team modal Name field is required\n  2301→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. Name field is empty.\n  2302→- **Action**: User fills in Identifier prefix \"QA\" and clicks \"Create Team\" without entering a Name\n  2303→- **Expected**: A validation error is displayed indicating the Name field is required. The modal remains open. No team is created.\n  2304→\n  2305→#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix is required\n  2306→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. Identifier field is empty.\n  2307→- **Action**: User fills in Name \"Quality Assurance\" and clicks \"Create Team\" without entering an Identifier prefix\n  2308→- **Expected**: A validation error is displayed indicating the Identifier prefix is required. The modal remains open. No team is created.\n  2309→\n  2310→#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix must be uppercase\n  2311→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n  2312→- **Action**: User types \"eng\" in the Identifier prefix field\n  2313→- **Expected**: The input is automatically converted to uppercase \"ENG\", or a validation error is shown indicating the prefix must be uppercase.\n  2314→\n  2315→#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix must be 2-5 characters\n  2316→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n  2317→- **Action**: User enters \"A\" (1 char) in the Identifier prefix field and clicks \"Create Team\"\n  2318→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the prefix must be between 2 and 5 characters. The modal remains open.\n  2319→\n  2320→#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix rejects more than 5 characters\n  2321→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n  2322→- **Action**: User enters \"TOOLONG\" (7 chars) in the Identifier prefix field and clicks \"Create Team\"\n  2323→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the prefix must be between 2 and 5 characters, or the input is limited to 5 characters. The modal remains open.\n  2324→\n  2325→#### Test: Create team modal Identifier prefix must be unique\n  2326→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. A team with identifier prefix \"ENG\" already exists.\n  2327→- **Action**: User enters Name \"Engineering 2\", Identifier prefix \"ENG\", and clicks \"Create Team\"\n  2328→- **Expected**: An error message is shown indicating the identifier prefix is already in use (e.g., \"A team with prefix 'ENG' already exists\"). The modal remains open. No duplicate team is created.\n  2329→\n  2330→#### Test: Create team with all fields filled\n  2331→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. Workspace has 2 existing teams.\n  2332→- **Action**: User enters Name \"Quality Assurance\", Identifier prefix \"QA\", Description \"QA team for testing\", and clicks \"Create Team\"\n  2333→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The teams page now shows the new \"Quality Assurance\" team card with prefix \"QA\", member count of 0 (or 1), and no active cycle. The team is persisted (reloading shows the team).\n  2334→\n  2335→#### Test: Create team with only required fields\n  2336→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n  2337→- **Action**: User enters Name \"DevOps\", Identifier prefix \"OPS\", leaves Description empty, and clicks \"Create Team\"\n  2338→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The new \"DevOps\" team card appears on the teams page with prefix \"OPS\" and no description issue.\n  2339→\n  2340→#### Test: Cancel create team modal discards input\n  2341→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. User has entered Name \"Test Team\", Identifier prefix \"TT\".\n  2342→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  2343→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new team is created. The teams list remains unchanged.\n  2344→\n  2345→#### Test: Close create team modal by clicking backdrop\n  2346→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open.\n  2347→- **Action**: User clicks outside the modal (on the backdrop overlay)\n  2348→- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating a team.\n  2349→\n  2350→#### Test: Create team modal form resets on reopen\n  2351→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`. User previously opened the Create Team modal, entered some data, and cancelled.\n  2352→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\" button again\n  2353→- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields empty/reset. No residual data from the previous attempt is present.\n  2354→\n  2355→#### Test: Create team modal can be used multiple times in sequence\n  2356→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/teams`.\n  2357→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Team\", enters Name \"Team Alpha\", prefix \"ALPH\", clicks \"Create Team\". Then clicks \"Create Team\" again, enters Name \"Team Beta\", prefix \"BETA\", clicks \"Create Team\".\n  2358→- **Expected**: Both teams are created. The teams page shows both new team cards. The modal opens cleanly with empty fields the second time.\n  2359→\n  2360→#### Test: Create team modal submits via Enter key\n  2361→- **Initial state**: Create Team modal is open. User has entered Name \"QA Team\" and Identifier prefix \"QA\".\n  2362→- **Action**: User presses Enter while focused on the form\n  2363→- **Expected**: The form is submitted, same behavior as clicking \"Create Team\". The team is created if all validations pass.\n  2364→\n  2365→### TeamSettings\n  2366→\n  2367→#### Test: Team settings page renders with editable fields\n  2368→- **Initial state**: Workspace has a team \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\" and description \"Core engineering team\". User clicks the \"Engineering\" team card on `/settings/teams`.\n  2369→- **Expected**: The team settings view displays: Team name field showing \"Engineering\" (inline editable), Identifier prefix field showing \"ENG\" (inline editable), Description field showing \"Core engineering team\" (inline editable), and a \"Team Members\" section listing current members. A \"Back\" or navigation link to return to the teams list is visible. A \"Delete Team\" button is also present.\n  2370→\n  2371→#### Test: Inline edit team name\n  2372→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2373→- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, changes it from \"Engineering\" to \"Platform Engineering\", and confirms (blur or Enter)\n  2374→- **Expected**: The team name updates to \"Platform Engineering\". The change is persisted (reloading the page still shows \"Platform Engineering\"). The sidebar team section also reflects the updated name.\n  2375→\n  2376→#### Test: Inline edit team name with empty value rejected\n  2377→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2378→- **Action**: User clicks on the team name field, clears the value, and attempts to confirm\n  2379→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the team name cannot be empty. The name reverts to \"Engineering\" or the error blocks the save.\n  2380→\n  2381→#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix\n  2382→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\".\n  2383→- **Action**: User clicks on the identifier prefix field, changes it to \"ENGR\", and confirms\n  2384→- **Expected**: The identifier prefix updates to \"ENGR\". The change is persisted. Existing issues retain their original identifiers (e.g., \"ENG-42\" does not change), but new issues will use the new prefix \"ENGR\".\n  2385→\n  2386→#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix enforces uppercase and 2-5 char limit\n  2387→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\".\n  2388→- **Action**: User clicks on the identifier prefix field and enters \"a\" (lowercase, 1 char)\n  2389→- **Expected**: The input is either auto-uppercased to \"A\" or rejected as lowercase. A validation error indicates the prefix must be 2-5 uppercase characters. The prefix reverts to \"ENG\" if the edit is not valid.\n  2390→\n  2391→#### Test: Inline edit team identifier prefix rejects duplicate prefix\n  2392→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with prefix \"ENG\". Another team \"Design\" has prefix \"DES\".\n  2393→- **Action**: User changes the identifier prefix from \"ENG\" to \"DES\" and confirms\n  2394→- **Expected**: An error is shown indicating the prefix \"DES\" is already in use by another team. The prefix reverts to \"ENG\" or the save is blocked.\n  2395→\n  2396→#### Test: Inline edit team description\n  2397→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with description \"Core engineering team\".\n  2398→- **Action**: User clicks on the description field, changes it to \"Platform and infrastructure engineering\", and confirms\n  2399→- **Expected**: The description updates to \"Platform and infrastructure engineering\". The change is persisted.\n  2400→\n  2401→#### Test: Inline edit team description can be cleared\n  2402→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\" with description \"Core engineering team\".\n  2403→- **Action**: User clicks on the description field, clears all text, and confirms\n  2404→- **Expected**: The description is cleared. The field shows a placeholder or empty state. No error is shown (description is optional).\n  2405→\n  2406→#### Test: Team members section lists all current team members\n  2407→- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2408→- **Expected**: The Team Members section displays a list of 3 members. Each member row shows their avatar and name. An \"Add Member\" button is visible.\n  2409→\n  2410→#### Test: Add member to team via team settings\n  2411→- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 2 members. Workspace member \"David\" is not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2412→- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\", selects \"David\" from the member selector, and confirms\n  2413→- **Expected**: David is added to the team. The Team Members section now shows 3 members including David. The team card on the teams page reflects the updated member count. David's member row on the Members page (`/settings/members`) now includes an \"Engineering\" team badge.\n  2414→\n  2415→#### Test: Add member selector shows only non-team members\n  2416→- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has members Alice and Bob. Workspace also has Carol and David who are not on this team. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2417→- **Action**: User clicks \"Add Member\"\n  2418→- **Expected**: The member selector dropdown shows only Carol and David (members not already on the team). Alice and Bob are not shown in the dropdown since they are already team members.\n  2419→\n  2420→#### Test: Remove member from team via team settings\n  2421→- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members: Alice, Bob, Carol. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2422→- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to Carol's name in the Team Members list\n  2423→- **Expected**: A confirmation prompt appears (e.g., \"Remove Carol from Engineering?\"). User confirms. Carol is removed from the team members list. The section now shows 2 members. Carol remains a workspace member but is no longer on the \"Engineering\" team. The team card member count decreases.\n  2424→\n  2425→#### Test: Cancel remove member from team\n  2426→- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 3 members. User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2427→- **Action**: User clicks the remove button next to a member's name, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation prompt\n  2428→- **Expected**: The member is not removed. The Team Members list still shows 3 members.\n  2429→\n  2430→#### Test: Team members section shows empty state when team has no members\n  2431→- **Initial state**: Team \"QA\" has no members. User is on team settings for \"QA\".\n  2432→- **Expected**: The Team Members section shows an empty state message (e.g., \"No members yet. Add members to this team.\"). The \"Add Member\" button is visible.\n  2433→\n  2434→#### Test: Add member to team can be done multiple times in sequence\n  2435→- **Initial state**: Team \"Engineering\" has 1 member. Workspace has 3 other members (Bob, Carol, David). User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2436→- **Action**: User adds Bob via \"Add Member\", then adds Carol via \"Add Member\" again\n  2437→- **Expected**: Both Bob and Carol are added to the team. The Team Members section now shows 3 members. The \"Add Member\" selector correctly filters out already-added members each time.\n  2438→\n  2439→#### Test: Delete team button shows confirmation dialog\n  2440→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2441→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Delete Team\" button\n  2442→- **Expected**: A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to delete the team 'Engineering'? This action cannot be undone.\"). The dialog has \"Confirm\" (or \"Delete\") and \"Cancel\" buttons. The team is NOT deleted yet.\n  2443→\n  2444→#### Test: Confirm delete team removes the team and navigates back\n  2445→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\". The delete confirmation dialog is open. Workspace has 3 teams.\n  2446→- **Action**: User clicks \"Confirm\" (or \"Delete\") in the confirmation dialog\n  2447→- **Expected**: The team \"Engineering\" is deleted. The user is navigated back to `/settings/teams`. The teams page now shows 2 team cards. \"Engineering\" no longer appears. The sidebar no longer shows the \"Engineering\" team section. Issues that belonged to this team are handled gracefully (either reassigned or still accessible).\n  2448→\n  2449→#### Test: Cancel delete team keeps the team\n  2450→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\". The delete confirmation dialog is open.\n  2451→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog\n  2452→- **Expected**: The dialog closes. The team \"Engineering\" is not deleted. The user remains on the team settings page.\n  2453→\n  2454→#### Test: Back navigation from team settings returns to teams list\n  2455→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\".\n  2456→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Back\" link or navigation button\n  2457→- **Expected**: The user is navigated back to `/settings/teams` showing the full list of team cards.\n  2458→\n  2459→#### Test: Team settings changes are reflected in sidebar navigation\n  2460→- **Initial state**: User is on team settings for \"Engineering\". The sidebar shows \"Engineering\" as a team section.\n  2461→- **Action**: User changes the team name from \"Engineering\" to \"Platform\"\n  2462→- **Expected**: The sidebar team section header updates from \"Engineering\" to \"Platform\" without requiring a page reload.\n  2463→\n  2464→## Labels Page (`/settings/labels`)\n  2465→\n  2466→**Components**: LabelList, CreateLabel, EditDeleteLabel\n  2467→\n  2468→### LabelList\n  2469→\n  2470→#### Test: Labels page renders with list of all labels\n  2471→- **Initial state**: Workspace has 3 labels: \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (blue), \"Improvement\" (green). User navigates to `/settings/labels`.\n  2472→- **Expected**: The page displays a list of 3 labels. Each label row shows a colored dot matching the label's color, the label name, and the issue count using that label. A \"Create Label\" button is visible at the top of the page. The page title indicates \"Labels\".\n  2473→\n  2474→#### Test: Label row displays colored dot matching label color\n  2475→- **Initial state**: Workspace has a label \"Bug\" with color red (#ef4444). User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2476→- **Expected**: The \"Bug\" label row displays a circular colored dot with the exact red color (#ef4444) next to the label name.\n  2477→\n  2478→#### Test: Label row displays issue count for each label\n  2479→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" used by 5 issues, label \"Feature\" used by 12 issues, and label \"Docs\" used by 0 issues. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2480→- **Expected**: The \"Bug\" row shows count \"5\", the \"Feature\" row shows count \"12\", and the \"Docs\" row shows count \"0\". The count is clearly visible next to or below the label name.\n  2481→\n  2482→#### Test: Labels page shows empty state when no labels exist\n  2483→- **Initial state**: Workspace has no labels. User navigates to `/settings/labels`.\n  2484→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No labels yet. Create your first label to get started.\") with an icon. The \"Create Label\" button is still visible.\n  2485→\n  2486→#### Test: Each label row has edit and delete action buttons\n  2487→- **Initial state**: Workspace has 2 labels. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2488→- **Expected**: Each label row displays an edit button (pencil/edit icon) and a delete button (trash/delete icon). The buttons are visible on the row (or appear on hover).\n  2489→\n  2490→#### Test: Labels list updates after creating a new label\n  2491→- **Initial state**: Workspace has 2 labels. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2492→- **Action**: User creates a new label \"Enhancement\" with color purple via the Create Label form\n  2493→- **Expected**: The labels list now shows 3 labels, including the newly created \"Enhancement\" label with a purple dot and issue count of 0. The new label appears in the list without requiring a page reload.\n  2494→\n  2495→#### Test: Labels list updates after deleting a label\n  2496→- **Initial state**: Workspace has 3 labels: \"Bug\", \"Feature\", \"Improvement\". User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2497→- **Action**: User deletes the \"Improvement\" label (clicks delete, confirms)\n  2498→- **Expected**: The labels list now shows 2 labels. \"Improvement\" is no longer in the list. The remaining labels \"Bug\" and \"Feature\" are still displayed correctly.\n  2499→\n  2500→#### Test: Labels list updates after editing a label\n  2501→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" with red color. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2502→- **Action**: User edits \"Bug\" label, changing name to \"Defect\" and color to orange\n  2503→- **Expected**: The labels list now shows \"Defect\" with an orange colored dot instead of \"Bug\" with red. The issue count remains unchanged.\n  2504→\n  2505→#### Test: Label issue count reflects actual usage across issues\n  2506→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" used by 3 issues. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2507→- **Action**: User navigates to an issue, adds the \"Bug\" label to it, then navigates back to `/settings/labels`\n  2508→- **Expected**: The \"Bug\" label now shows issue count of 4, reflecting the newly tagged issue.\n  2509→\n  2510→### CreateLabel\n  2511→\n  2512→#### Test: Create Label button opens the create label form\n  2513→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2514→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Create Label\" button\n  2515→- **Expected**: A create label form (inline or modal) appears with a name text input field, a color picker section showing preset color options and a custom hex input, and \"Create\" and \"Cancel\" buttons.\n  2516→\n  2517→#### Test: Successfully create a new label with preset color\n  2518→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`. The create label form is open. Workspace has 2 existing labels.\n  2519→- **Action**: User types \"Bug\" in the name field, selects the red preset color, and clicks \"Create\"\n  2520→- **Expected**: The form closes. A new \"Bug\" label with red color appears in the labels list. The list now shows 3 labels. The new label has issue count 0.\n  2521→\n  2522→#### Test: Successfully create a new label with custom hex color\n  2523→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`. The create label form is open.\n  2524→- **Action**: User types \"Custom Category\" in the name field, enters \"#ff6b2e\" in the custom hex color input, and clicks \"Create\"\n  2525→- **Expected**: The form closes. A new \"Custom Category\" label appears in the labels list with the exact custom color (#ff6b2e) displayed as its colored dot.\n  2526→\n  2527→#### Test: Create label form validates required name field\n  2528→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`. The create label form is open.\n  2529→- **Action**: User leaves the name field empty and clicks \"Create\"\n  2530→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the name is required (e.g., \"Label name is required\"). The label is not created. The form remains open.\n  2531→\n  2532→#### Test: Create label form prevents duplicate label names\n  2533→- **Initial state**: Workspace has a label named \"Bug\". The create label form is open.\n  2534→- **Action**: User types \"Bug\" in the name field, selects a color, and clicks \"Create\"\n  2535→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"A label with this name already exists\"). The label is not created. The form remains open.\n  2536→\n  2537→#### Test: Cancel button closes create label form without creating\n  2538→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`. The create label form is open. User has typed \"Draft Label\" in the name field.\n  2539→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\"\n  2540→- **Expected**: The form closes. No new label is created. The labels list remains unchanged. If the user opens the form again, the name field is empty (form state is reset).\n  2541→\n  2542→#### Test: Color picker shows preset color options\n  2543→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`. The create label form is open.\n  2544→- **Expected**: The color picker displays a set of preset color swatches (e.g., red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple, pink, gray). Each swatch is clickable. A custom hex input field is also available.\n  2545→\n  2546→#### Test: Selecting a preset color updates the color preview\n  2547→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`. The create label form is open.\n  2548→- **Action**: User clicks the blue preset color swatch\n  2549→- **Expected**: The selected color swatch is visually highlighted (e.g., ring/border). A color preview (colored dot or swatch) updates to show the selected blue color. The custom hex input shows the blue hex value.\n  2550→\n  2551→#### Test: Custom hex input validates hex color format\n  2552→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings/labels`. The create label form is open.\n  2553→- **Action**: User types \"notacolor\" in the custom hex input and clicks \"Create\" with a valid name\n  2554→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown for the color field (e.g., \"Invalid color format\"). The label is not created.\n  2555→\n  2556→#### Test: Create label form can be used multiple times in sequence\n  2557→- **Initial state**: Workspace has 1 label. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2558→- **Action**: User creates label \"Bug\" (red) via the form, then opens the form again and creates label \"Feature\" (blue)\n  2559→- **Expected**: Both labels are created successfully. The labels list shows 3 labels total. The form resets correctly between uses — the second time the form opens, name field is empty and no color is pre-selected.\n  2560→\n  2561→### EditDeleteLabel\n  2562→\n  2563→#### Test: Clicking edit button on a label enters inline edit mode\n  2564→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red). User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2565→- **Action**: User clicks the edit button on the \"Bug\" label row\n  2566→- **Expected**: The label row transforms into an inline edit mode. The name field becomes an editable text input pre-filled with \"Bug\". The color picker appears showing the current red color as selected. \"Save\" and \"Cancel\" buttons appear on the row.\n  2567→\n  2568→#### Test: Successfully edit label name via inline edit\n  2569→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red) used by 3 issues. User is on `/settings/labels`. The \"Bug\" label is in inline edit mode.\n  2570→- **Action**: User clears the name field, types \"Defect\", and clicks \"Save\"\n  2571→- **Expected**: The label row exits edit mode. The label now shows \"Defect\" with the same red color. The issue count remains 3. Issues that had the \"Bug\" label now show \"Defect\" as their label.\n  2572→\n  2573→#### Test: Successfully edit label color via inline edit\n  2574→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red). User is on `/settings/labels`. The \"Bug\" label is in inline edit mode.\n  2575→- **Action**: User selects the blue preset color and clicks \"Save\"\n  2576→- **Expected**: The label row exits edit mode. The label now shows \"Bug\" with a blue colored dot. The color change is reflected anywhere the label appears (e.g., issue rows, issue detail label badges).\n  2577→\n  2578→#### Test: Edit both label name and color simultaneously\n  2579→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red). User is on `/settings/labels`. The \"Bug\" label is in inline edit mode.\n  2580→- **Action**: User changes the name to \"Critical Bug\", selects orange color, and clicks \"Save\"\n  2581→- **Expected**: The label row exits edit mode. The label now shows \"Critical Bug\" with an orange colored dot.\n  2582→\n  2583→#### Test: Cancel inline edit reverts changes\n  2584→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red). User is on `/settings/labels`. The \"Bug\" label is in inline edit mode.\n  2585→- **Action**: User changes name to \"Something Else\", selects blue color, then clicks \"Cancel\"\n  2586→- **Expected**: The label row exits edit mode. The label still shows \"Bug\" with red color. No changes are saved.\n  2587→\n  2588→#### Test: Edit label validates required name field\n  2589→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red). The \"Bug\" label is in inline edit mode.\n  2590→- **Action**: User clears the name field completely and clicks \"Save\"\n  2591→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown (e.g., \"Label name is required\"). The edit mode remains active. The label is not saved with an empty name.\n  2592→\n  2593→#### Test: Edit label prevents duplicate label names\n  2594→- **Initial state**: Workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red) and \"Feature\" (blue). The \"Bug\" label is in inline edit mode.\n  2595→- **Action**: User changes the name to \"Feature\" and clicks \"Save\"\n  2596→- **Expected**: An error message is shown (e.g., \"A label with this name already exists\"). The edit mode remains active. The label name is not changed.\n  2597→\n  2598→#### Test: Edit label with custom hex color\n  2599→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red). The \"Bug\" label is in inline edit mode.\n  2600→- **Action**: User enters \"#22c55e\" in the custom hex color input and clicks \"Save\"\n  2601→- **Expected**: The label row exits edit mode. The label \"Bug\" now displays a green colored dot matching #22c55e.\n  2602→\n  2603→#### Test: Clicking delete button shows confirmation dialog\n  2604→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red) used by 5 issues. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2605→- **Action**: User clicks the delete button on the \"Bug\" label row\n  2606→- **Expected**: A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to delete the label 'Bug'? This label is used by 5 issues.\"). The dialog has \"Confirm\" (or \"Delete\") and \"Cancel\" buttons. The label is NOT deleted yet.\n  2607→\n  2608→#### Test: Confirm delete removes the label\n  2609→- **Initial state**: Workspace has 3 labels including \"Bug\" (red) used by 5 issues. The delete confirmation dialog for \"Bug\" is open.\n  2610→- **Action**: User clicks \"Confirm\" (or \"Delete\") in the confirmation dialog\n  2611→- **Expected**: The label \"Bug\" is deleted. The labels list now shows 2 labels. The 5 issues that had the \"Bug\" label no longer have it (the label is removed from their label list). The label filter dropdowns on issue pages no longer include \"Bug\".\n  2612→\n  2613→#### Test: Cancel delete keeps the label\n  2614→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red). The delete confirmation dialog for \"Bug\" is open.\n  2615→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog\n  2616→- **Expected**: The dialog closes. The \"Bug\" label is not deleted. The labels list remains unchanged.\n  2617→\n  2618→#### Test: Delete label used by zero issues\n  2619→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Archived\" (gray) with 0 issues. User is on `/settings/labels`.\n  2620→- **Action**: User clicks delete on \"Archived\", confirmation dialog shows (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to delete the label 'Archived'?\"), user confirms\n  2621→- **Expected**: The label is deleted. The labels list no longer includes \"Archived\". No issues are affected since the label was unused.\n  2622→\n  2623→#### Test: Only one label can be in edit mode at a time\n  2624→- **Initial state**: Workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red) and \"Feature\" (blue). User is on `/settings/labels`. \"Bug\" is currently in inline edit mode.\n  2625→- **Action**: User clicks the edit button on \"Feature\"\n  2626→- **Expected**: \"Bug\" exits edit mode without saving changes. \"Feature\" enters inline edit mode. Only one label row is editable at a time.\n  2627→\n  2628→#### Test: Edit mode is exited when delete is clicked on same label\n  2629→- **Initial state**: Workspace has label \"Bug\" (red) in inline edit mode. User has changed name to \"Defect\" but not saved.\n  2630→- **Action**: User clicks the delete button on the \"Bug\" row\n  2631→- **Expected**: The inline edit mode is exited (unsaved changes are discarded). The delete confirmation dialog appears for \"Bug\" (the original name, not the unsaved \"Defect\").\n  2632→\n  2633→## Settings Page (`/settings`)\n  2634→\n  2635→**Components**: WorkspaceSettings\n  2636→\n  2637→### WorkspaceSettings\n  2638→\n  2639→#### Test: Settings page renders workspace name and default team fields\n  2640→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and navigates to `/settings`. Workspace is named \"My Workspace\" and has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\".\n  2641→- **Expected**: The page displays a \"Workspace name\" text input pre-filled with \"My Workspace\", and a \"Default team for new issues\" dropdown showing the currently configured default team. A page heading \"Settings\" is visible.\n  2642→\n  2643→#### Test: Edit workspace name inline\n  2644→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings`. Workspace name is \"My Workspace\".\n  2645→- **Action**: User clears the workspace name field, types \"Acme Corp\", and clicks the \"Save\" button (or presses Enter)\n  2646→- **Expected**: The workspace name is updated to \"Acme Corp\". A success confirmation is shown (e.g., toast or inline message). The sidebar workspace header updates to reflect the new name \"Acme Corp\".\n  2647→\n  2648→#### Test: Workspace name cannot be saved as empty\n  2649→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings`. Workspace name is \"My Workspace\".\n  2650→- **Action**: User clears the workspace name field entirely and attempts to save\n  2651→- **Expected**: A validation error is shown indicating the workspace name is required. The save action is prevented. The workspace name remains \"My Workspace\".\n  2652→\n  2653→#### Test: Edit workspace name and verify persistence after navigation\n  2654→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings`. Workspace name is \"My Workspace\".\n  2655→- **Action**: User changes workspace name to \"New Name\" and saves. Then user navigates to `/my-issues` via the sidebar and navigates back to `/settings`.\n  2656→- **Expected**: The workspace name field shows \"New Name\", confirming the change was persisted to the database.\n  2657→\n  2658→#### Test: Change default team for new issues\n  2659→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings`. Teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" exist. Default team is set to \"Engineering\".\n  2660→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Default team for new issues\" dropdown and selects \"Design\". User clicks \"Save\".\n  2661→- **Expected**: The default team is updated to \"Design\". A success confirmation is shown. When the user opens the Create Issue modal from any page, the team selector defaults to \"Design\".\n  2662→\n  2663→#### Test: Default team dropdown lists all available teams\n  2664→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings`. Workspace has teams \"Engineering\", \"Design\", and \"QA\".\n  2665→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Default team for new issues\" dropdown\n  2666→- **Expected**: The dropdown shows all three teams: \"Engineering\", \"Design\", and \"QA\".\n  2667→\n  2668→#### Test: Change default team and verify it affects issue creation\n  2669→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings`. Default team is \"Engineering\". Teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\" exist.\n  2670→- **Action**: User changes default team to \"Design\" and saves. User navigates to `/team/design/issues` and clicks the \"New Issue\" button.\n  2671→- **Expected**: The Create Issue modal opens with the team selector defaulted to \"Design\".\n  2672→\n  2673→#### Test: Settings page is accessible from sidebar navigation\n  2674→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`. Sidebar is visible.\n  2675→- **Action**: User clicks \"Settings\" (with settings icon) in the Workspace section of the sidebar\n  2676→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings`. The Settings page loads with workspace settings fields.\n  2677→\n  2678→#### Test: Workspace name edit can be cancelled\n  2679→- **Initial state**: User is on `/settings`. Workspace name is \"My Workspace\".\n  2680→- **Action**: User changes the workspace name field to \"Changed Name\" but navigates away without saving (e.g., clicks \"My Issues\" in sidebar)\n  2681→- **Expected**: The workspace name remains \"My Workspace\" (unsaved changes are discarded). Returning to `/settings` shows the original name.\n  2682→\n  2683→#### Test: Settings page shows appropriate heading and layout\n  2684→- **Initial state**: User navigates to `/settings`\n  2685→- **Expected**: The page has a clear \"Settings\" heading. The workspace name field and default team dropdown are displayed in a clean form layout consistent with the app's dark theme. Fields have labels clearly indicating their purpose.\n  2686→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EEhVNodsZKH9PoDNCi8fg2","session_id":"6a47338b-4185-45a1-b5fc-e067e9bff431","uuid":"c55006d1-21d0-4483-aca3-0700dc49bf93"}
